of Funds sides of the nine domestic sectors and the rest of the world, everything issued is the Liabilities side of all domestic sectors, NT$ million, yearly at 31 December","note":"Every owner is a sector of the flow of funds that Taiwan's central bank publishes once a year, at market value, in New Taiwan dollars, for 31 December; each year's figures arrive about thirteen months later. Households are what is left once the other sectors are counted, so they carry any error in the others. Non-residents are holders who live outside Taiwan. The national pension sits with the government, Chunghwa Post's savings with the banks, and mutual funds with the other financial firms. Government securities are central and local government bonds and Treasury bills, at market value. The central bank holds none; its own paper is counted separately. Source: Central Bank of the Republic of China (Taiwan), Flow of Funds, used under the Open Government Data License, version 1.0; shares of the total are our calculations."}